```

Simplest: module singleton with start/stop refcount, or class instantiated once. I'll make a singleton `cpuStore` with `start()` returning stop. React component calls start/stop in effect; with StrictMode double effect it restarts — guard with listener count: start only when first subscriber, stop when last leaves.

Live tick: setInterval 1000ms → appendPoint(now, value). To keep it robust in background tabs: compute how many steps elapsed since last point and fill that many (gap → nulls if > e.g. 10 missed, else random-walk fill). Keep it simple: each tick, catch up to now with per-second points; if missed > 30s, insert nulls.

Value model: `v = clamp(base(t) + noise)`; noise = random walk. Spikes: occasional jump to 85-100 for a few minutes.

